WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.080
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday. It's punishment Tuesday.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.980
Henry... remember how you came up with this really gross meal for me?

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:10.680
[Henry] Slobber carrots with me drool, and gross barbecue with me drool.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.500
Gross barbecue with me drool, gross slobber carrots with me drool... and hat.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.840
[Henry] Not with you!

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.260
No, *you*. You- your drool.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:17.760
[Henry] Yeah.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.540
Hm. I would prefer my drool.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:20.400
[Henry] Why?

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.500
My drool's already in my mouth.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.600
Couple questions, Henry. First off, what are slobber carrots?

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.280
[Henry] They are cooked carrots.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.620
Okay, that doesn't sound too bad.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.460
And then barbecue's basically just meat and barbecue sauce, right?

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:32.460
[Henry] Yes.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:33.680
I mean, I gotta say.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.420
So far, the only gross part of this sounds like it's gonna be your drool.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.740
[Henry] Here's the luncheon loaf!

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:39.500
...Uh, oh.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.740
[John] Henry, what do you think luncheon loaf is gonna taste like?

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.000
[Henry] You know, like goo!

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.660
They're so focused on value they didn't even

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.120
spend the money to print the "e" in value!

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.360
Okay, so we're making slobber carrots.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.640
First thing you need to do is preheat the oven.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.080
Henry! What temperature should we preheat the oven to?

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.520
[Henry] Four, two... five!

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.140
425! Sounds good.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.700
I wonder if Mom helped you out with that.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.840
We're gonna take out the salt and pepper.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.560
Henry, do you wanna be Mr. Salt, or Mr. Pepper?

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.540
[Henry] Mr. Salt!

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.100
Okay.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.120
[John] These are becoming... fairly well-seasoned slobber carrots here, buddy.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.720
Okay, I think that's definitely enough.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.660
Henry, do you wanna go ahead and drool on the carrots now,

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:14.660
or after they're cooked?

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:15.620
[Henry] Now!

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.940
[Henry blows raspberries]

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.180
Oh... that's...

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.440
[Henry] What's a luncheon loaf?

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.880
[John] It's a meat-like product.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.380
And then it should just... OH!

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:26.960
Oh, God, that looks horrible.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.060
[grunts loudly]

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.520
[Henry] That has to be superhuman strength!

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.180
BRRRRR!

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.920
[John] It just looks delicious.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.020
Do you wanna know something interesting, Henry?

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:37.520
[Henry] What?

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:40.080
[John] The first ingredient of Valu Time Luncheon Loaf

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.500
is mechanically separated chicken, comma, pork.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:44.980
[Henry] Pork...?

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.560
[John] And then the last ingredient... is smoke flavoring.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.580
I didn't know that was an ingredient!

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.140
[Sarah] How does it smell, Henry?

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.960
[Henry] Just... eewie!

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.200
So, what you wanna do now is you wanna

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.600
cut a couple slices of Valu Time luncheon loaf.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.300
I am *not* looking forward to having that in my body.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.440
You wanna cook it over a low heat, aaand...

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.460
Also, it's time to put in the slobber carrots.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:05.460
Alright!

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.060
Oh... we need a hat!

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.640
Henry, what should we make a hat out of?

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:10.840
[Henry] Cabbage!

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.660
Cabbage? That's a great idea!

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.060
So, Henry, when you're making a cabbage hat,

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:17.480
the key is to let Mom cut the cabbage.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.260
[Sarah] We're also cooking coleslaw.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.640
So, here's my cabbage hat.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.240
Oh, yeah.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.980
Alright, you ready for my cabbage hat trick?

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:24.620
[Henry] Yeah.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.660
Whoa! [Henry laughs]

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:28.520
Whoa! [Henry giggles]

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.780
Aw, I did it!

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:36.980
So, once your luncheon loaf is reasonably browned, you put it on a plate of its own.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.840
[John] Alright, Henry, it's time to put on the barbecue sauce!

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:39.960
Isn't that enough?

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.180
...Oh.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:43.000
Oh, my.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.060
And, of course, the last ingredient you need iiis... drool.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:46.860
[Henry blows raspberries]

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.420
[John] Oh, just a tiny little sprinkling of drool.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.800
Lastly, you're going to want to take your slobber carrots out of the oven.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:52.860
We're ready to eat.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.600
So, you take the cabbage hat... whoop! Bam.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:58.540
Then, you take your barbecue with Valu Time Luncheon Loaf...

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.900
Oh, that is... that looks delicious.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.380
[Henry] No, it doesn't.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.900
[John] Aaand, on top go the slobber carrots.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.780
[Henry] This is gonna be the grossest meal!

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:11.420
First, I'm gonna try the slobber carrots with drool.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:14.300
It's actually quite good.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.720
If anything, the drool *adds* something.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.380
Gross barbecue with drool... okay.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.100
[Baby Alice coos offscreen]

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:18.940
[gags]

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.420
[mouth full] It's so bad...

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.040
[fork clatters]

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:35.800
[John] Uuugh...

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.680
So much worse than a blenderized Happy Meal.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:40.520
[loud sigh]

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.540
[Sarah] What about hat?

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.040
...Alright, I'll have a little bit of hat.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:44.960
That's okay.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.120
Oh... not very good.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.060
[Sarah] Oh? [Alice coos]

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.040
So, there you have it, Hank, that was my punishment meal.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.540
Uh... I don't recommend it.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.120
It was, to quote Henry, the grossest meal ever.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.160
I'll see you on Friday.

